From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:13:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: report a Moonlight client waiting for its PIN in
 heartbeats

Moonlight starts pairing with getservercert and keeps the request open
until the host user types the PIN the client shows. Upstream only flips
the tray icon (no tray in a desk). The HTTP thread now marks the waiting
request (client address, since) and the heartbeat carries it as
"pairing": null or {"address","since"} (docs/contracts/ipc.md), so
the service can ask for the PIN in one place and the console tray can
notify the owner.

The mark goes when nvhttp::pin() hands the PIN over, when the pairing
session is removed (finished, failed, replaced) and, as a last resort,
after five minutes: Sunshine never notices a client that gave up.

